### Title
Rattler default on fresh installations and upgrades

### Why
Conda 26.10 switches the default solver to rattler. Existing solver choices must
remain effective, and the packaged installation must include the solver plugin.

### Platforms
- [ ] Windows
- [ ] macOS
- [ ] Linux

### Prerequisites
Use disposable installations with the 26.10 release candidate packages and
`conda-rattler-solver >=26.10.1`. Also prepare conda 26.9 installations with no
solver setting and with explicit `libmamba`, `classic`, and `pycosat` settings.

### Steps
1. In a fresh 26.10 installation, run `conda config --show solver` and `conda info`.
2. Create an environment with `conda create --name solver-check python`, then
   install and remove a package in that environment without passing `--solver`.
3. Upgrade each 26.9 installation to the 26.10 release candidate. Repeat the
   configuration check and package operations.
4. In the installation without a solver setting, repeat a package operation
   with `--solver=libmamba` and `--solver=classic`.

### Pass criteria
Fresh installations and upgrades without a solver setting select rattler.
Explicit solver settings survive the upgrade. Package operations succeed with
the default and explicitly selected solvers.

### Out of scope / notes
Configuration precedence is covered by `test_configured_solver_backend`.
This scenario checks packaged solver availability and upgrades on each platform.
